  m_text: "The compact disc (CD) is a digital optical disc data storage format co-developed
    by Philips and Sony to store and play digital audio recordings. \r\n\r\nFirst
    released in Japan in October 1982, the CD was the second optical disc format
    to reach the market, following the larger LaserDisc (LD). \r\n\r\n As of 2007,
    over 200 billion CDs (including audio CDs, CD-ROMs, and CD-Rs) had been sold
    worldwide. "
